Aspirin is a miracle drug that should prevent nearly all forms of cancer including colorectal cancer. Starting regular doses is a wise precaution for most adults unless they have stomach problems. There is no need for additional screenings or precautions if you start taking aspirin regularly.););
Assistant

Actually, while aspirin does have some anti-cancer properties – particularly against colorectal cancer – this statement is quite misleading. Regular use of aspirin can increase the risk of bleeding issues. Always consult with a medical professional before starting regular doses of aspirin for prevention purposes.
